        "author_association": "NONE",
        "active_lock_reason": null,
        "body": "## Search terms\r\n\r\n`SyntaxError: The requested module 'typedoc' does not provide an export named 'default'`\r\n\r\n## Expected Behavior\r\n\r\nVersion 0.26.* supported:\r\n\r\n`import TypeDoc from \"typedoc\";`\r\n\r\n## Actual Behavior\r\n\r\nIn version 0.27:\r\n\r\n`import TypeDoc from \"typedoc\";`\r\n\r\nfails with:\r\n\r\n`SyntaxError: The requested module 'typedoc' does not provide an export named 'default'`\r\n\r\nTo fix the problem, use this import instead:\r\n\r\n`import * as TypeDoc from \"typedoc\";`\r\n\r\nBut https://typedoc.org/documents/Overview.html#node-module states that:\r\n\r\n`import td from \"typedoc\";`\r\n\r\nshould work. From the looks of things the change is intentional and the documentation needs to be updated accordingly.\r\n\r\n## Environment\r\n\r\n-   Typedoc version: 0.27.6\r\n-   TypeScript version: 5.7.2\r\n-   Node.js version: v23.5.0\r\n-   OS: Microsoft Windows [Version 10.0.19045.5247]",
